  "goodToKnow": "Kollektiv means collective: kollektive Verantwortung, das kollektive Gedächtnis (collective memory), important in German Erinnerungskultur. Das Kollektiv is a collective group, and in the GDR, Arbeitskollektive were work teams, so the word can sound East German. Germans also discuss Kollektivschuld (collective guilt) after the Nazi era, a concept many reject in favour of collective responsibility. Stressed on the last syllable."
